{"title": "Sectional Mock #71 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>What is the area of a quadrilateral ABCD, (shown below) in which sides AB and BC are equal, sides AD and CD are of lengths 5 cm and 13 cm, respectively, and side AD is perpendicular to the diagonal AC?</p><p><img width=255 height=161 id=\"Picture 30\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27933/image023.png\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, (&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;) &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AB &#2324;&#2352; BC &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AD &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AD &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; AC &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=255 height=161 id=\"Picture 30\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27933/image023.png\" ></p>", "options_en": ["75 cm&#178;", "78 cm&#178;", "82 cm&#178;", "80 cm&#178;"], "options_hi": ["75 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;", "78 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;", "82 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;", "80 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>&#916;ADC: AD &#8869; AC, AD = 5, CD = 13, AC = &radic;(13&#178; - 5&#178;) = 12</p><p>Area &#916;ADC = (1/2)  X  12  X  5 = 30 cm&#178;</p><p>&#916;ABC: AB = BC, AC = 12</p><p>Area via Heron's: s = (10+10 + 12) / 2 = 16, Area = &radic;(16(6)(6)(4)]= 48cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total area = 30+48= 78 cm&#178;</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#916;ADC: AD &#8869; AC, AD = 5, CD = 13, AC = &radic;(13&#178; - 5&#178;) = 12</p><p>Area &#916;ADC = (1/2)  X  12  X  5 = 30 cm&#178;</p><p>&#916;ABC: AB = BC, AC = 12</p><p>Area via Heron's: s = (10+10 + 12) / 2 = 16, Area = &radic;(16(6)(6)(4)]= 48cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total area = 30+48= 78 cm&#178;</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two points S and T are in a river and R is in between S and T such that SR = 63 km and river flow along TS. If a boat start travelling from point R to T and then return to point S in total of 45 hours and the boat can travel 108 km in still water in Y hours and the speed of the stream is 4.2 km/h, then what is the value of Y? (ST = 120 km)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; S &#2324;&#2352; T &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; R, S &#2324;&#2352; T &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; SR = 63 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2342;&#2368; TS &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2348;&#2361;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; R &#2360;&#2375; T &#2340;&#2325; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 45 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; S &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; Y &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 108 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 4.2 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (ST = 120 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;)</p>", "options_en": ["15", "16", "18", "20"], "options_hi": ["15", "16", "18", "20"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of the boat in still water = 108/Y</p><p>and speed of stream = 4.2 km/h</p><p>So, upstream speed = (108/Y  -  4.2) km/h</p><p>And downstream speed = (108/Y + 4.2) km/h</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>57/(108/Y + 4.2) + 120/(108/Y  -  4.2) = 45</p><p>=&gt; Y = 15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of the boat in still water = 108/Y</p><p>and speed of stream = 4.2 km/h</p><p>So, upstream speed = (108/Y  -  4.2) km/h</p><p>And downstream speed = (108/Y + 4.2) km/h</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>57/(108/Y + 4.2) + 120/(108/Y  -  4.2) = 45</p><p>=&gt; Y = 15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many whole numbers lie between 11<sup>2</sup> and 12<sup>2</sup>? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>11<sup>2</sup> &#2324;&#2352; 12<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;? </p>", "options_en": ["23", "24", "21", "22"], "options_hi": ["23", "24", "21", "22"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Numbers lie between 11<sup>2</sup> and 12<sup>2 </sup>= 144 - 121 - 1 = 22. </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Numbers lie between 11<sup>2</sup> and 12<sup>2 </sup>= 144 - 121 - 1 = 22. </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the compound interest (in &#8377;) on a sum of &#8377; 7,500 for 4 years if the rate of interest is 20% per annum for the first two years and 10% per annum for the next two years. (The interest is compounded annually.)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 20% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 10% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377; 7,500 &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;? (&#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;)</p>", "options_en": ["6,558", "5,658", "5,586", "5,568"], "options_hi": ["6,558", "5,658", "5,586", "5,568"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Compound interest for first two years = 7500[(1 + 20/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 7500[(6/5)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 7500[(36-25)/25]</p><p>= 300 * 11</p><p>= &#8377;3300</p><p>Compound interest for next two years = 7500 + 3300 = 10800</p><p>Compound interest for next two years = 10800[(1 + 10/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 10800[(11/10)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 10800[(121-100)/100]</p><p>= 108 * 21</p><p>= &#8377;2268</p><p>Total compound interest = 3300 + 2268 = &#8377;5568</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Compound interest for first two years = 7500[(1 + 20/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 7500[(6/5)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 7500[(36-25)/25]</p><p>= 300 * 11</p><p>= &#8377;3300</p><p>Compound interest for next two years = 7500 + 3300 = 10800</p><p>Compound interest for next two years = 10800[(1 + 10/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 10800[(11/10)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 10800[(121-100)/100]</p><p>= 108 * 21</p><p>= &#8377;2268</p><p>Total compound interest = 3300 + 2268 = &#8377;5568</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>P, Q and R started a hotel. Three times the investment of Q is equal to seven times the investment of P and is equal to twice the investment of R. If the total annual profit earned by them is 20.5 lakhs, then what is the difference between profit share (in lakhs) of Q and R?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;&#2335;&#2354; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;, P &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2340; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; R &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 20.5 &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; (&#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2.1", "3.5", "2.5", "4.1"], "options_hi": ["2.1", "3.5", "2.5", "4.1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the investment of Q = Rs. a</p><p>Then, investment of P = 3a/7</p><p>Investment of R = 3a/2</p><p>Period of investment for P, Q and R is same. So,</p><p>Now, profit ratio = investment ratio, P: Q: R = (3a/7): a: (3a/2) = 6: 14: 21</p><p>Total profit earned = 20.5 lakhs</p><p>Therefore, difference between share of Q and R = [(21  -  14)/(6 + 14 + 21)] * 20.5 = <b>3.5 lakhs</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the investment of Q = Rs. a</p><p>Then, investment of P = 3a/7</p><p>Investment of R = 3a/2</p><p>Period of investment for P, Q and R is same. So,</p><p>Now, profit ratio = investment ratio, P: Q: R = (3a/7): a: (3a/2) = 6: 14: 21</p><p>Total profit earned = 20.5 lakhs</p><p>Therefore, difference between share of Q and R = [(21  -  14)/(6 + 14 + 21)] * 20.5 = <b>3.5 lakhs</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A right circular cone is 6.4 cm high with a radius of its base of 5 cm. It is melted and recast into a right circular cone with the radius of its base 4 cm. Find its height.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 6.4 cm &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 5 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 4 cm &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2338;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10 cm", "5 cm", "20 cm", "12 cm"], "options_hi": ["10 cm", "5 cm", "20 cm", "12 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the required height be h cm.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><img width=171 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23800/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=81 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23800/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23800/image003.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the required height be h cm.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><img width=171 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23800/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=81 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23800/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23800/image003.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of G<sup>3</sup> + H<sup>3</sup> + I<sup>3</sup>, if G + H + I = 0?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; G + H + I = 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; G<sup>3</sup> + H<sup>3</sup> + I<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["G<sup>2</sup> + H<sup>2</sup> + I<sup>2</sup>  -  3GHI", "0", "3GHI", "1"], "options_hi": ["G<sup>2</sup> + H<sup>2</sup> + I<sup>2</sup> - 3GHI", "0", "3GHI", "1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We know that, if (a + b + c) = 0, then a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> = 3abc.</p><p>So,</p><p>G<sup>3</sup> + H<sup>3</sup> + I<sup>3 </sup>= 3GHI</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that, if (a + b + c) = 0, then a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> = 3abc.</p><p>So,</p><p>G<sup>3</sup> + H<sup>3</sup> + I<sup>3 </sup>= 3GHI</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the 3<sup>rd</sup> term of a geometric progression is -21 and common ratio is 3 then 5<sup>th</sup> term of the series is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2379;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2339;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2342; -21 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["-486", "-189", "-148", "-729"], "options_hi": ["-486", "-189", "-148", "-729"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>3<sup>rd</sup> term = -21</p><p>ar<sup>2</sup> = -21</p><p>a x 9 = -21</p><p>a = -7/3</p><p>5<sup>th</sup> term = ar<sup>4</sup></p><p>= (-7/3) x (3)<sup>4</sup></p><p>= -7 x 27 = -189</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3<sup>rd</sup> term = -21</p><p>ar<sup>2</sup> = -21</p><p>a x 9 = -21</p><p>a = -7/3</p><p>5<sup>th</sup> term = ar<sup>4</sup></p><p>= (-7/3) x (3)<sup>4</sup></p><p>= -7 x 27 = -189</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If a = c +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a = c +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["2c/(4c<sup>2</sup> + 1)", "4c/(4c<sup>2</sup> + 1)", "2c/(2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)", "2c/(2c<sup>2</sup> + 2)"], "options_hi": ["2c/(4c<sup>2</sup> + 1)", "4c/(4c<sup>2</sup> + 1)", "2c/(2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)", "2c/(2c<sup>2</sup> + 2)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>a = c + 1/2c</p><p>a = (2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)/2c</p><p>Now a<sup>-1</sup> = 1/a = 1/[(2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)/2c] = 2c/(2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a = c + 1/2c</p><p>a = (2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)/2c</p><p>Now a<sup>-1</sup> = 1/a = 1/[(2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)/2c] = 2c/(2c<sup>2</sup> + 1)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>If sin&#952; = 11/12, then what will be the value of (tan&#952; + sec&#952;)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; sin&#952; = 11/12, &#2340;&#2379; (tan&#952; + sec&#952;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;23", "11/&radic;23", "12/&radic;23", "23"], "options_hi": ["&radic;23", "11/&radic;23", "12/&radic;23", "23"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>sin &#952; = 11/12 </p><p>Since, sin<sup>2</sup> &#952; + cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 1</p><p>cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 1  -  (11/12)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 1  -  121/144 </p><p>cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 23/144</p><p>cos&#952; = &radic;23/12</p><p>tan&#952; + sec&#952; = sin&#952;/cos&#952; + 1/cos&#952; </p><p>= (11/12)/(&radic;23/12) + 1/(&radic;23/12) </p><p>= 11/&radic;23 + 12/&radic;23 </p><p>= 23/&radic;23 </p><p>= &radic;23</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>sin &#952; = 11/12 </p><p>Since, sin<sup>2</sup> &#952; + cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 1</p><p>cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 1  -  (11/12)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 1  -  121/144 </p><p>cos<sup>2</sup> &#952; = 23/144</p><p>cos&#952; = &radic;23/12</p><p>tan&#952; + sec&#952; = sin&#952;/cos&#952; + 1/cos&#952; </p><p>= (11/12)/(&radic;23/12) + 1/(&radic;23/12) </p><p>= 11/&radic;23 + 12/&radic;23 </p><p>= 23/&radic;23 </p><p>= &radic;23</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Shanu marks up his good by 25% and gives a discount of 15%. Apart from this, he uses a faulty balance also, which reads 1000 gm for 750 gm. what is his profit percentage?(rounded off to two decimal places)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2370; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 25% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2379;&#2359;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2370; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2368; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; 750 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 1000 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;)</p>", "options_en": ["35%", "42%", "50%", "55%"], "options_hi": ["35%", "42%", "50%", "55%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Shanu marks up his goods by 25%</p><p>Discount allows = 15%</p><p>Uses faulty weight that reads 1000 grams when it actually weighs only 750 grams.</p><p>Let Cost price = Rs. C</p><p>Marked price = C * (1 + 0.25) = 1.25C</p><p>Selling price = MP(1  -  0.15) = 1.25C * 0.85 = 1.0625C</p><p>Effective selling price = SP/0.75 = 1.0625C/0.75 </p><p>=&gt; 1.42C(approx.)</p><p>Net profit = 1.42C  -  C = 0.42C</p><p>Required profit percentage = 0.42C/C * 100 = 42%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Shanu marks up his goods by 25%</p><p>Discount allows = 15%</p><p>Uses faulty weight that reads 1000 grams when it actually weighs only 750 grams.</p><p>Let Cost price = Rs. C</p><p>Marked price = C * (1 + 0.25) = 1.25C</p><p>Selling price = MP(1  -  0.15) = 1.25C * 0.85 = 1.0625C</p><p>Effective selling price = SP/0.75 = 1.0625C/0.75 </p><p>=&gt; 1.42C(approx.)</p><p>Net profit = 1.42C  -  C = 0.42C</p><p>Required profit percentage = 0.42C/C * 100 = 42%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, find &#8736;HGF.</p><p><img width=399 height=286 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/742891/image007.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;HGF &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"399\" height=\"286\" id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/742891/image007.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["18&deg;", "19&deg;", "21&deg;", "23&deg;"], "options_hi": ["18&deg;", "19&deg;", "21&deg;", "23&deg;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>&#8736;CAB = 180  -  129 = 51, </p> <p>&#8736;ABC = 180  -  110 = 70,</p> <p>&#8736;ACB = &#8736;ECF = (180  -  51  -  70) = 59</p> <p>&#8736;CEF = 180  -  121 = 59</p> <p>&#8736;CFE = &#8736;FHG + &#8736;HGF = 62</p> <p>=&gt; &#8736;HGF = 21&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8736;CAB = 180  -  129 = 51, </p> <p>&#8736;ABC = 180  -  110 = 70,</p> <p>&#8736;ACB = &#8736;ECF = (180  -  51  -  70) = 59</p> <p>&#8736;CEF = 180  -  121 = 59</p> <p>&#8736;CFE = &#8736;FHG + &#8736;HGF = 62</p> <p>=&gt; &#8736;HGF = 21&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>A path of width 'r/24' m is made outside and around a square field of side 'r' m. If the area of the path is 400 m<sup>2</sup>, then find the value of 'r'.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>'r/24' &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2341; 'r' &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 400 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'r' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["35", "21", "48", "56"], "options_hi": ["35", "21", "48", "56"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Side of square field = 'r' m</p><p>side of square field with path = r + r/24 + r/24 = 13r/12 m</p><p>Area of the path = 400 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>(13r/12)<sup>2</sup>  -  r<sup>2</sup> = 400</p><p>25r<sup>2</sup>/144 = 400</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 2304</p><p>r = 48 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Side of square field = 'r' m</p><p>side of square field with path = r + r/24 + r/24 = 13r/12 m</p><p>Area of the path = 400 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>(13r/12)<sup>2</sup>  -  r<sup>2</sup> = 400</p><p>25r<sup>2</sup>/144 = 400</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 2304</p><p>r = 48 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">5.21<sup>3</sup> - 2.21<sup>3</sup>", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">5.21<sup>3</sup> - 2.21<sup>3</sup>", "options_en": ["-1", "-2", "-3", "2"], "options_hi": ["-1", "-2", "-3", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=360 height=165 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18726/image034.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=360 height=165 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18726/image034.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of three adjacent faces of a cuboidal box is 120 cm<sup>2</sup>, 72 cm<sup>2</sup> and 60 cm<sup>2</sup>, respectively. Find the volume (in cm<sup>3</sup>) of the box.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349;&#2368;&#2351; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2310;&#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2330;&#2375;&#2361;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 120 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>, 72 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2324;&#2352; 60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["425", "650", "720", "864"], "options_hi": ["425", "650", "720", "864"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>&#183; lb = 120 cm<sup>2</sup>, bh = 72 cm<sup>2</sup>, hl = 60 cm<sup>2</sup> </p><p><sup>&#183; </sup>(lb)(bh)(hl) = (l * b * h)&#178; = 120  X  72  X  60 = 60<sup>2</sup>  X  12<sup>2</sup></p><p><sup>&#183; </sup>Volume of the box = l  X  b  X  h = &radic;(60<sup>2</sup>  X  12<sup>2</sup>) = 720 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#183; lb = 120 cm<sup>2</sup>, bh = 72 cm<sup>2</sup>, hl = 60 cm<sup>2</sup> </p><p><sup>&#183; </sup>(lb)(bh)(hl) = (l * b * h)&#178; = 120  X  72  X  60 = 60<sup>2</sup>  X  12<sup>2</sup></p><p><sup>&#183; </sup>Volume of the box = l  X  b  X  h = &radic;(60<sup>2</sup>  X  12<sup>2</sup>) = 720 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;If 10X<sup>2</sup> + 11X + 10 = 0, then the value of X<sup>3</sup> + (<div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 10X<sup>2</sup> + 11X + 10 = 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; X<sup>3</sup> + (<div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "options_en": ["2", "4", "8", "5"], "options_hi": ["2", "4", "8", "5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=131 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image032.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=83 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image035.png\"></p><p><img width=107 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=187 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=175 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=161 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=104 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image042.png\"></p><p><img width=132 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image043.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=131 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image032.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=83 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image035.png\"></p><p><img width=107 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=187 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=175 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=161 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=104 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image042.png\"></p><p><img width=132 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image043.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>60% of the villagers are illiterate from which 80% are female. Total males in the village are 40%. What percentage of villagers are literate males?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>60% &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368;&#2339; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 80% &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 40% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368;&#2339; &#2360;&#2366;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["28%", "32%", "40%", "16%"], "options_hi": ["28%", "32%", "40%", "16%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let total number of villagers = 100</p><p>Illiterate villagers = 60% of 100 = 60</p><p>Illiterate females = 60 * 80/100 = 48</p><p>Illiterate males = 60  -  48 = 12</p><p>Total number of males = 40% of 100 = 40</p><p>Number of literate male employees = 40  -  12 = 28</p><p>Required percentage = 28/100 * 100 = 28%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let total number of villagers = 100</p><p>Illiterate villagers = 60% of 100 = 60</p><p>Illiterate females = 60 * 80/100 = 48</p><p>Illiterate males = 60  -  48 = 12</p><p>Total number of males = 40% of 100 = 40</p><p>Number of literate male employees = 40  -  12 = 28</p><p>Required percentage = 28/100 * 100 = 28%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>X and Y are two stations which are 280 km apart. A train starts at a certain time from X and travels towards Y at 60 km/h. After 2 hours, another train starts from Y and travels towards X at 20 km/h. After how much time from the start of train which left from X, both trains meet?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 280 km &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2358;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; X &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; 60 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; Y &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; X &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; 20 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["4 hours", "3 hours", "6 hours", "2 hours"], "options_hi": ["4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Distance covered by the train leaving from X in 2 hr = 60 * 2 = 120 km</p><p>Remaining distance = 280 - 120 = 160 km</p><p>Now, relative speed = 60 + 20 = 80 km/hr</p><p>Time in which both trains meet after the train leaving from Y started = 160/80 = 2 hr</p><p>Required time = 2 + 2 = 4 hr</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance covered by the train leaving from X in 2 hr = 60 * 2 = 120 km</p><p>Remaining distance = 280 - 120 = 160 km</p><p>Now, relative speed = 60 + 20 = 80 km/hr</p><p>Time in which both trains meet after the train leaving from Y started = 160/80 = 2 hr</p><p>Required time = 2 + 2 = 4 hr</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B and C started a business by investing amounts in the ratio of 5: 4: 3 respectively. A invested for 16 months which is 1 month and 6 months more than the investment period of B and C respectively. What is the ratio of profit earned by A, B and C respectively?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;: 5:4:3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; A &#2344;&#2375; 16 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8: 6: 3", "4: 3: 2", "8: 9: 5", "4: 2: 1"], "options_hi": ["8: 6: 3", "4: 3: 2", "8: 9: 5", "4: 2: 1"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let Rs.5a, Rs.4a and Rs.3a are amounts invested by A, B and C respectively.</p><p>A's investment period = 16 months</p><p>B's investment period = 16  -  1 = 15 months</p><p>C's investment period = 16  -  6 = 10 months</p><p>Therefore, profit ratio = A: B: C = (5a * 16): (4a * 15): (3a * 10) = <b>8: 6: 3</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Rs.5a, Rs.4a and Rs.3a are amounts invested by A, B and C respectively.</p><p>A's investment period = 16 months</p><p>B's investment period = 16  -  1 = 15 months</p><p>C's investment period = 16  -  6 = 10 months</p><p>Therefore, profit ratio = A: B: C = (5a * 16): (4a * 15): (3a * 10) = <b>8: 6: 3</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a park, there are goats and hens in the ratio 7: 11. If legs are counted, the total number of legs is 500. Find the number of goats.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2325;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; 7:11 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 500 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2325;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["70", "56", "77", "84"], "options_hi": ["70", "56", "77", "84"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of goats and hens be 7X and 11X respectively.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>7X * 4 + 11X * 2 = 500</p><p>50X = 500</p><p>X = 10</p><p>Number of goats = 7X = 70</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of goats and hens be 7X and 11X respectively.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>7X * 4 + 11X * 2 = 500</p><p>50X = 500</p><p>X = 10</p><p>Number of goats = 7X = 70</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following statement is true?</p><p>I. 6<sup>4</sup> X 5<sup>5</sup> is even</p><p>II. 4<sup>5</sup> X 7<sup>5</sup> is even</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>I. 6<sup>4</sup> X 5<sup>5</sup> &#2360;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;|</p><p>II. 4<sup>5</sup> X 7<sup>5</sup> &#2360;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;|</p>", "options_en": ["Only II", "Both I and II", "Neither I nor II", "Only I"], "options_hi": ["&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II", "I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;", "&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>I. 6<sup>4</sup> X 5<sup>5</sup></p><p>When an even number is multiplied by another even number then their solution will be even. So, 6<sup>4</sup> will be even.</p><p>Similarly, when an odd number is multiplied by another odd number then their solution will be odd. So, 5<sup>5</sup> will be odd.</p><p>Multiplication of an even and an odd number always given an even value.</p><p>So, 6<sup>4</sup> X 5<sup>5</sup>is even.</p><p>Hence, statement I is true.</p><p>II. 4<sup>5</sup> X 7<sup>5</sup></p><p>When an even number is multiplied by another even number then their solution will be even. So, 4<sup>5</sup> will be even.</p><p>Similarly, when an odd number is multiplied by another odd number then their solution will be odd. So, 7<sup>5</sup> will be odd.</p><p>Multiplication of an even and an odd number always given an even value.</p><p>So, 4<sup>5</sup> X 7<sup>5</sup> is even.</p><p>Hence, statement II is true.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>I. 6<sup>4</sup> X 5<sup>5</sup></p><p>When an even number is multiplied by another even number then their solution will be even. So, 6<sup>4</sup> will be even.</p><p>Similarly, when an odd number is multiplied by another odd number then their solution will be odd. So, 5<sup>5</sup> will be odd.</p><p>Multiplication of an even and an odd number always given an even value.</p><p>So, 6<sup>4</sup> X 5<sup>5</sup>is even.</p><p>Hence, statement I is true.</p><p>II. 4<sup>5</sup> X 7<sup>5</sup></p><p>When an even number is multiplied by another even number then their solution will be even. So, 4<sup>5</sup> will be even.</p><p>Similarly, when an odd number is multiplied by another odd number then their solution will be odd. So, 7<sup>5</sup> will be odd.</p><p>Multiplication of an even and an odd number always given an even value.</p><p>So, 4<sup>5</sup> X 7<sup>5</sup> is even.</p><p>Hence, statement II is true.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If cot A = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>3", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cot A = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>3", "options_en": ["16/49", "9/49", "9/16", "16/9"], "options_hi": ["16/49", "9/49", "9/16", "16/9"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>cosec<sup>2</sup>A/sec<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup>A/sin<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= cot<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= (3/7)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 9/49</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>cosec<sup>2</sup>A/sec<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= cos<sup>2</sup>A/sin<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= cot<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= (3/7)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 9/49</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person borrowed a sum of &#8377;8,000 at an interest rate of 10% p.a., compounded semi-annually. What is the compound interest for a period of 1 year?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#8377;8,000 &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 10% &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2368;&#2404; 1 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;820", "&#8377;1,600", "&#8377;1,680", "&#8377;800"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;820", "&#8377;1,600", "&#8377;1,680", "&#8377;800"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Since the rate is compounded semi-annually.</p><p>Effective rate of interest = 10/2 = 5%</p><p>Effective time period = 1 * 2 = 2</p><p>Required compound interest = 8000 * [(1 + 5/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 8000 * (41/400)</p><p>= &#8377;820</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since the rate is compounded semi-annually.</p><p>Effective rate of interest = 10/2 = 5%</p><p>Effective time period = 1 * 2 = 2</p><p>Required compound interest = 8000 * [(1 + 5/100)<sup>2</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 8000 * (41/400)</p><p>= &#8377;820</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the equation of a line parallel to 2m + 7n = 3 and passing through point (2,1).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2m + 7n = 3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; (2,1) &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2325;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2332;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3m + 2n  -  4 = 0", "4m + n + 6 = 0", "2m + 7n  -  11 = 0", "2m + n  -  3 = 0"], "options_hi": ["3m + 2n - 4 = 0", "4m + n + 6 = 0", "2m + 7n - 11 = 0", "2m + n - 3 = 0"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The equation of a line parallel to 2m + 7n = 3 can be written as -</p><p>2m + 7n = k</p><p>Since, the line passes through (2,1).</p><p>2*2 + 7*1 = k</p><p>k = 4 + 7 = 11</p><p>Therefore, the equation is 2m + 7n  -  11 = 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The equation of a line parallel to 2m + 7n = 3 can be written as -</p><p>2m + 7n = k</p><p>Since, the line passes through (2,1).</p><p>2*2 + 7*1 = k</p><p>k = 4 + 7 = 11</p><p>Therefore, the equation is 2m + 7n  -  11 = 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A trader sells sugar at its cost price but cheats by weighing X% more while buying and 10% less while selling. If his overall profit was 20%, then find the value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; X% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; 10% &#2325;&#2350; &#2340;&#2380;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2343;&#2379;&#2326;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 20% &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10%", "17%", "8%", "12%"], "options_hi": ["10%", "17%", "8%", "12%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=316 height=76 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27562/image004.png\"></p><p>Profit percentage = 20</p><p>[(100 + X  -  90)/90]*100 = 20</p><p>10 + X = 18</p><p>X = 8%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=316 height=76 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27562/image004.png\"></p><p>Profit percentage = 20</p><p>[(100 + X  -  90)/90]*100 = 20</p><p>10 + X = 18</p><p>X = 8%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}]}